WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:02.820
You know the setting sun?

00:02.820 --> 00:05.970
They say that it's at the end 
of a long tunnel.

00:06.540 --> 00:10.250
You have to overcome all sorts of dangers,

00:10.250 --> 00:13.560
so we'll have to learn lots
 of magic to be prepared.

00:14.450 --> 00:19.290
<i>When you talked about your dreams, 
your eyes glittered like jewels.</i>

00:20.180 --> 00:24.820
<i>You were so blindingly brilliant, 
and I was hopelessly weak.</i>

00:24.820 --> 00:27.460
Elfie, I know you'll be able to make it.

00:27.460 --> 00:29.130
But me...

00:29.130 --> 00:30.380
<i>Even so...</i>

00:33.030 --> 00:35.010
Will, it won't do if you're not with me!

00:37.350 --> 00:40.780
If you won't be there,
then there's no point!

00:43.280 --> 00:46.120
So... let's go together.

00:49.160 --> 00:50.530
<i>It's been five years since then.</i>

00:52.220 --> 00:55.440
<i>And now, I'm headed to where you are.</i>

01:15.050 --> 01:19.770
Episode 18
The First Bloom

02:30.590 --> 02:34.260
<b>Noble Quarter, High-End Clothier Les Aile</b>

02:32.660 --> 02:35.480
The principles of wisdom, 
attunement, and scholarship...

02:35.920 --> 02:38.500
are held in high esteem by
Rigarden Magical Academy,

02:38.500 --> 02:42.050
and only those who embody all three

02:42.050 --> 02:47.800
are permitted to wear the mark
of high mages, the colorless Gloria.

02:49.320 --> 02:51.460
They look wonderful on you.

02:50.770 --> 02:56.410
<b>Tenth Proprietor of the Lesaile Boutique
Brandtal les Aile</b>

02:51.460 --> 02:54.930
To have overseen the robes you will wear 
as you take flight into your futures...

02:54.930 --> 02:56.660
is quite an honor.

02:58.670 --> 03:00.640
They're so light and easy to move in!

03:00.640 --> 03:02.910
And to think they're resistant
 to magic, too!

03:02.910 --> 03:06.540
The academy cloaks were 
magnificent defensive equipment,

03:06.540 --> 03:08.420
but these are clearly superior.

03:08.420 --> 03:12.160
Mages really do excel 
in crafting such things.

03:12.160 --> 03:13.860
They're even perfectly tailored.

03:13.860 --> 03:18.550
Just like the previous proprietor, 
you do good work, Brandtal.

03:18.550 --> 03:21.580
I'm honored, Master Sion.

03:21.580 --> 03:26.060
My apologies they were not ready
until the day you set out for the tower.

03:26.060 --> 03:27.780
It's not your fault.

03:27.780 --> 03:31.700
With what happened at Terminalia, 
everyone's been set back.

03:33.790 --> 03:36.820
So this is the special garb 
for ascending the tower, is it?

03:37.700 --> 03:39.320
Julius, what's wrong?

03:39.600 --> 03:41.680
You've seemed kind of down 
for a while now.

03:41.680 --> 03:44.100
Shut up! Just leave me alone!

03:47.940 --> 03:49.910
Colette, you...

03:49.910 --> 03:52.670
You detestable lord of destruction!

03:52.670 --> 03:54.040
I-I'm sorry!

03:54.040 --> 03:56.030
I'm so very sorry!

03:56.030 --> 03:58.740
It's no trouble at all. 
Please, just leave everything as it is.

03:58.740 --> 04:00.680
I'm sorry!

04:03.380 --> 04:06.060
Julius really is acting strangely,
 isn't he?

04:06.060 --> 04:09.100
Colette, have you been 
scouted by the tower?

04:09.750 --> 04:13.570
I did receive a letter from
 the earth faction some time ago.

04:13.570 --> 04:17.330
For me, the lightning faction. 
For Wignall, the elves.

04:17.330 --> 04:21.300
For Sion, fire. We've all been scouted.

04:21.300 --> 04:24.090
Only Julius hasn't received an offer.

04:24.510 --> 04:26.200
That's what's bothering him.

04:26.200 --> 04:28.670
And now, the finishing touch...

04:29.430 --> 04:32.030
Our shop has had the privilege

04:32.030 --> 04:36.360
of preparing more than a few Gloria 
for those setting out for the tower.

04:36.840 --> 04:41.440
May the protection 
of the Mage Queen be with you.

04:41.840 --> 04:44.430
By the way, what happened to Will?

04:44.430 --> 04:46.180
I haven't seen him.

04:46.180 --> 04:51.000
If you're referring to Mister Serfort, 
he visited our shop prior to you.

04:51.000 --> 04:54.110
He seemed to be in quite 
a hurry and left quickly.

04:55.070 --> 04:56.360
Right now, I'm sure he's...

04:56.360 --> 04:58.050
with Mister Donnan!

04:56.440 --> 04:59.110
<b>Slumland Street
Donnan's Forge</b>

05:03.960 --> 05:05.370
Look, Will.

05:05.370 --> 05:07.550
Your new sword.

05:07.550 --> 05:12.120
I took your broken Moria blade, 
added a Wist gem, and reforged it.

05:12.530 --> 05:14.620
It'll cut through magic 
just like it always did,

05:14.620 --> 05:18.160
and it can amplify the magic stored 
in the gems around the capital.

05:19.130 --> 05:22.130
I guess you'd call it Wist-set silver.

05:22.130 --> 05:24.120
Wist-set silver...

05:25.510 --> 05:30.740
I was confident in your last sword too,
and you went and broke it!

05:30.740 --> 05:33.590
Your monstrous strength 
is enough to shame a dwarf!

05:34.260 --> 05:35.900
I'm sorry, Mister Donnan.

05:36.180 --> 05:39.900
Thank you. Um, how much do I owe you?

05:39.900 --> 05:43.610
I don't need your money. 
This is thanks for saving all of us.

05:43.610 --> 05:44.280
What?

05:44.280 --> 05:47.040
Do your best out there, sword-wizard.

05:47.040 --> 05:48.910
It may be the tower, but go run riot!

05:50.040 --> 05:51.040
Yes, sir!

05:51.790 --> 05:53.610
Hey, there he is!

05:54.290 --> 05:58.100
Will! Are you ready?

05:58.100 --> 05:59.780
Yeah. Sorry to keep you waiting.

05:59.780 --> 06:01.550
Well then, let's go!

06:01.550 --> 06:02.810
To the tower!

06:10.030 --> 06:12.810
Looks like the fifty of you 
are here, right?

06:12.810 --> 06:16.060
All those brand-new Gloria 
are blinding me!

06:16.350 --> 06:20.630
We're severely shorthanded right now, 
so I'll be the only one attending you,

06:20.630 --> 06:23.570
but I'll do the job right, 
so don't you worry!

06:24.950 --> 06:27.950
Is she really a high mage?

06:27.950 --> 06:30.950
Well then, it looks like
 you're all raring to go,

06:32.720 --> 06:34.720
so why don't we get right to it?

06:35.960 --> 06:41.140
Welcome to a paradise of research 
and a strict hell,

06:41.140 --> 06:42.970
my new little fledglings!

06:47.490 --> 06:51.260
It's thanks to you that 
I made it this far, Rosty.

06:52.030 --> 06:53.980
I'm on my way, Elfie!

07:01.110 --> 07:03.330
What is this place?

07:03.330 --> 07:04.660
There's nothing here.

07:04.990 --> 07:05.980
Access...

07:05.980 --> 07:07.480
Clairie Serah.

07:07.990 --> 07:09.660
Gate Unlock.

07:11.790 --> 07:13.500
The ceiling's opening up!

07:13.500 --> 07:14.900
That's not all.

07:14.900 --> 07:16.000
This is...

07:16.000 --> 07:17.940
The floor we're standing on is moving.

07:17.940 --> 07:20.250
No, it's rising!

07:24.210 --> 07:28.930
<b>Tower, First Floor: Colorless Garden</b>

07:26.080 --> 07:29.340
Whoa! This is amazing!

07:29.850 --> 07:33.220
A white... No, a colorless city?

07:33.220 --> 07:36.810
There's a sky! And a horizon! 
There's even light!

07:36.810 --> 07:38.480
Rose, you'll fall!

07:38.480 --> 07:40.880
E-Even the castle is floating.

07:40.880 --> 07:44.840
This can't be real, can it? 
Are we really inside the tower?

07:45.290 --> 07:49.110
Behold the first floor of the tower, 
the Colorless Garden!

07:49.110 --> 07:51.950
When outsiders talk
 about the Upper Institute,

07:51.950 --> 07:54.870
they're generally referring
 to the facilities on this level.

07:54.870 --> 07:59.810
It supports the tower from the bottom up,
providing the foundation for life here.

07:59.810 --> 08:04.310
It's also an academic center
 for researching and developing new magic.

08:04.310 --> 08:08.320
Only those acknowledged 
by the academy may enter here.

08:08.320 --> 08:11.140
For mages, it is a realm of glory!

08:12.390 --> 08:14.400
I'm so happy for us!

08:15.140 --> 08:19.900
Whether you become permanent 
residents here or not is up to you.

08:24.780 --> 08:26.440
Well, let's go!

08:26.440 --> 08:29.000
You're all today's special guests!

08:29.000 --> 08:31.780
Everyone's waiting at the hall
 for the ceremony!

08:33.530 --> 08:37.220
Wignall, are the light and sky here...

08:37.220 --> 08:38.370
Yes.

08:38.370 --> 08:41.160
No doubt elven illusion magic.

08:41.160 --> 08:43.790
Likely very advanced, at that.

08:44.100 --> 08:46.300
This is amazing!

08:46.850 --> 08:48.500
Will, look! Look!

08:49.430 --> 08:53.550
So many people are wearing
 the same Gloria we are!

08:54.110 --> 08:56.390
There's a morrie garden! 
All those magical herbs!

08:56.390 --> 08:59.770
And is that a testing site 
for magical creatures over there?

08:59.770 --> 09:03.870
This really is the front line 
of magical research!

09:03.870 --> 09:08.880
It's a little late, but this really makes 
me feel like I've become a high mage!

09:08.880 --> 09:09.650
Yeah.

09:10.070 --> 09:12.160
It truly is like a dream.

09:13.290 --> 09:14.160
And...

09:14.160 --> 09:16.120
they even have a crêpe shop!

09:16.540 --> 09:17.950
Owen Sique...

09:17.950 --> 09:19.160
Lisolde Dua!

09:19.540 --> 09:20.290
Algiz!

09:21.740 --> 09:22.860
Five of them?

09:22.860 --> 09:25.910
Knights never go back on their word. 
Also, I don't require any change.

09:25.910 --> 09:28.670
Hey! What are you doing, Lihanna?!

09:28.670 --> 09:31.770
We're in the middle of the tower
entrance ceremony right now!

09:31.770 --> 09:33.830
This is no time to be eating, is it?

09:33.830 --> 09:35.050
Come on! Let's go!

09:35.690 --> 09:37.860
I see Lihanna's just the same as always.

09:37.860 --> 09:40.530
Indeed, that voracious appetite of hers...

09:40.530 --> 09:42.810
At this point, it's almost refreshing.

09:43.560 --> 09:44.440
You're right.

09:45.690 --> 09:47.820
Don't get too excited, laggard.

09:48.820 --> 09:52.820
The tower isn't the bright,
 friendly place you take it for.

09:53.210 --> 09:54.660
What do you mean?

10:01.900 --> 10:06.750
<i>He's right. The way the high mages 
are staring at us feels kind of...</i>

10:07.420 --> 10:11.170
Blast it! So the rumors were true?

10:11.170 --> 10:13.750
<i>At this rate, we'll also...</i>

10:14.550 --> 10:17.300
<b>The Gate of Pruning</b>

10:16.110 --> 10:17.300
Here we are!

10:17.640 --> 10:19.600
Now, go right on in!

10:21.890 --> 10:24.810
<b>The Pruning Ceremonial Hall</b>

10:25.530 --> 10:27.280
This is the ceremonial hall?

10:28.380 --> 10:29.440
There's earth,

10:29.770 --> 10:30.940
wind,

10:31.290 --> 10:32.440
darkness...

10:32.780 --> 10:35.210
Mages from each of the factions are here?

10:35.210 --> 10:36.330
Somehow...

10:36.700 --> 10:40.380
The way they're looking at us 
feels a little scary.

10:37.120 --> 10:40.830
<b>Director of the Upper Institute & Head of the Colorless Faction
Kreutz Harlon</b>

10:43.460 --> 10:44.580
That's...

10:54.300 --> 10:56.470
<b>Magia Vander Albis Vina
Five Supreme Wands, Icemaiden's Wand & Head of the Ice Faction
Elfaria Albis Serfort</b>

10:56.970 --> 10:59.140
<b>Magia Vander Thorzeus Fasce
Five Supreme Wands, Lightning Lord's Wand & Head of the Lightning Faction
Zeo Thorzeus Reinbolt</b>

10:59.600 --> 11:01.850
<b>Magia Vander Incindia Barham
Five Supreme Wands, Flame Emperor's Wand & Head of the Fire Faction
Cariot Incindia Wiseman</b>

11:01.850 --> 11:04.600
<b>Magia Vander Elleaf Canaan
Five Supreme Wands, Sacred Elf's Wand & Head of the Elf Faction
Ellenor Ljos Alf</b>

11:06.470 --> 11:07.600
<i>Ellenor!</i>

11:12.670 --> 11:14.730
<i>Elfie! Sorry I kept you waiting!</i>

11:17.590 --> 11:18.760
<i>Elfie?</i>

11:22.540 --> 11:29.210
Thank you for all you do from high 
atop the tower, noble Magia Vander!

11:29.210 --> 11:31.460
This little chore is a tired custom.

11:31.460 --> 11:37.090
Please move things along efficiently 
so we don't get bored, Miss Clairie.

11:38.690 --> 11:41.980
You really have moved up in the world, 
haven't you, my dear junior?

11:41.980 --> 11:45.230
I'm already used to your 
condescending manner.

11:46.510 --> 11:49.280
Well, I had delightful upperclassmen 
who worked me very hard!

11:49.280 --> 11:50.870
Lord Cariot.

11:50.870 --> 11:52.480
I know, Logwell.

12:01.990 --> 12:05.970
Now, just as the 
Magia Vander have requested,

12:05.970 --> 12:09.120
let's get right into the First Bloom!

12:09.120 --> 12:10.420
First Bloom?

12:10.900 --> 12:13.360
First, beginning with 
the Grand Magic Festival,

12:13.360 --> 12:18.130
some little fledglings have been scouted 
over their six years at the academy!

12:18.130 --> 12:21.760
They shall now be bestowed
with what we call the Blessing of Color!

12:40.530 --> 12:41.620
Blast it.

12:46.910 --> 12:50.460
<b>Fire Faction
Sion Ulster</b>

12:51.000 --> 12:54.460
<b>Lightning Faction
Lihanna Owenzaus</b>

12:54.920 --> 12:58.470
<b>Elf Faction
Wignall Lindor</b>

12:59.090 --> 13:02.470
<b>Earth Faction
Colette Loire</b>

13:02.470 --> 13:05.340
My Gloria's turned red!

13:05.340 --> 13:07.720
Mine's dark brown!

13:07.720 --> 13:11.230
And my brooch! It became
 the emblem of the earth faction!

13:18.830 --> 13:20.180
Does this mean...

13:23.640 --> 13:26.160
<i>Mine has no color!</i>

13:27.240 --> 13:28.500
<b>Synthesis Wand</b>

13:28.620 --> 13:32.000
<b><u>Kreutz Harlon</u>

Race: Rhizanth   Age: 28   Height: 176 cm
Birthday: 23rd of Nullsmoon
Likes: Research, experiments, dissection
Dislikes: Wasted time, inefficient progress, obtuse people
Object of Pursuit Akin to a First Love:
The current magical world, so distorted and contradictory
yet so beautiful</b>

13:28.620 --> 13:32.000
<b>Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 28th
Equipment: Synthesis wand, Uraglaine, magic items
Skills: Water and wind magic; developing magic items and creatures

 A Word from the Great Icemaiden's Wand, Albis Vina, Lady Elfaria Albis Serfort:
"Because you interfered with my love letters to Will, I hate you!!!"</b>

13:33.710 --> 13:37.000
<b><u>Colorless Garden</u>

It's a paradise for artificers and researchers.
For mages who aim to become Magia Vander, it's a graveyard of disgrace.

The colorless faction? Nothing more than a collection of the jobless.

-Words of scorn from a certain high mage</b>

13:37.000 --> 13:39.260
<b>One Day Earlier</b>

13:38.230 --> 13:40.510
Sarissa, you liar!

13:40.940 --> 13:47.510
You said that if Will ascended to the 
tower, I'd be allowed to scout him!

13:47.760 --> 13:50.430
Stop fussing like a child.

13:51.100 --> 13:54.590
All sorts of things are plainly visible.
Please straighten yourself up.

13:55.750 --> 13:59.750
You said I couldn't do it while Will 
was still in school, so I held back!

13:59.750 --> 14:01.260
If he proved himself capable,

14:01.260 --> 14:04.660
weren't you and the rest of the faction 
supposed to accept him?!

14:04.660 --> 14:08.660
All those love letters— 
I mean, scouting offers I wrote to Will!

14:09.050 --> 14:12.180
It's <i>your</i> fault that they 
never reached him, isn't it?

14:12.180 --> 14:14.290
Just how many did you write?

14:14.290 --> 14:18.360
And that wasn't my doing.
 It was the Upper Institute.

14:19.630 --> 14:22.670
By the Upper Institute, 
do you mean Kreutz?

14:22.670 --> 14:23.980
Yes.

14:23.980 --> 14:27.210
He wouldn't interject an opinion 
about the academy's decisions,

14:27.210 --> 14:30.720
however, he still has doubts about letting
 the likes of a sword join a faction.

14:30.720 --> 14:33.110
He said he would not permit
the boy to be scouted.

14:33.770 --> 14:37.460
May I pop over to the Upper Institute 
and encase everything in ice?

14:37.460 --> 14:38.440
Don't you dare!

14:39.790 --> 14:41.730
Please calm yourself.

14:41.730 --> 14:45.290
If he's able to prove himself
at the First Bloom, I have their word.

14:45.290 --> 14:47.200
Kreutz and the others will accept him.

14:47.480 --> 14:49.660
The tower is an extreme meritocracy.

14:49.660 --> 14:51.830
Lady Elfaria, if you recruited him now,

14:51.830 --> 14:55.460
it would destroy people's 
perception of Will Serfort.

14:55.860 --> 15:00.720
As an outlier, he must first earn 
the entire tower's acknowledgment.

15:01.380 --> 15:05.580
As for Clairie and the legwork with the
 other factions, I will take care of that.

15:06.790 --> 15:10.820
Or do you think that he won't be able 
to make full use of his skills?

15:12.360 --> 15:14.140
I don't think that.

15:14.500 --> 15:17.290
If I know Will, 
he'll definitely overcome this.

15:18.040 --> 15:21.900
This Blessing of Color itself 
is a prestigious award!

15:21.900 --> 15:25.650
Now, go to the factions that await you!

15:26.340 --> 15:30.680
I hope that even one of you
reach the greatest heights of the tower!

15:48.270 --> 15:49.050
What?

15:49.470 --> 15:50.980
Wait...

15:50.980 --> 15:53.600
We haven't been awarded anything.

15:54.160 --> 15:58.220
<i>After it made such a huge impression,
that welcoming blessing...</i>

15:58.220 --> 16:03.860
Now, those of you who've reached the tower
 but not been blessed are "colorless."

16:04.140 --> 16:06.110
In other words, worthless.

16:06.510 --> 16:10.860
Only faction-aligned mages 
can reach the top of the tower.

16:10.860 --> 16:13.620
None else are permitted to proceed.

16:14.200 --> 16:17.870
So what was leaked only 
to high-ranking nobles was true.

16:18.160 --> 16:22.800
Those who can't join a faction remain 
on the first floor permanently

16:22.800 --> 16:24.570
as mere scrap to the tower.

16:25.120 --> 16:28.880
They exist only as cogs
to support outstanding high mages.

16:29.160 --> 16:32.660
The nickname for the tower 
in the shadow of its glory...

16:33.340 --> 16:36.390
is the wand graveyard.

16:36.390 --> 16:37.400
What?

16:38.140 --> 16:39.140
However...

16:40.400 --> 16:44.500
As you've made it all the way to the 
tower, you'll all be given a chance!

16:44.500 --> 16:49.880
Demonstrate your ability here and now,
and a faction may yet recruit you!

16:50.280 --> 16:53.740
This is the main event of the First Bloom!

16:53.740 --> 16:56.540
If you haven't been able 
to prove yourself before today,

16:56.950 --> 17:00.290
then now is the time to show 
your colors! Burst into bloom!

17:02.220 --> 17:03.920
Don't tell me that's...

17:04.750 --> 17:06.160
a monster?

17:07.420 --> 17:10.110
There is only one rule in the tower.

17:10.110 --> 17:11.810
Prove your worth!

17:12.680 --> 17:15.680
Let the First Bloom begin!

17:15.680 --> 17:17.520
Blast it!

17:20.270 --> 17:22.400
Your task is quite simple.

17:22.400 --> 17:24.770
Defeat those monsters.

17:25.190 --> 17:27.400
Fight using any techniques
 you've mastered.

17:27.400 --> 17:30.030
Throw bunches of flashy spells at them!

17:30.030 --> 17:33.160
Don't hold back in appealing
 to the factions, all right?

17:33.160 --> 17:35.820
E-Even if we're free to fight
however we want...

17:35.820 --> 17:38.540
Lyril! Right now, we just have to attack!

17:38.540 --> 17:40.500
Ignis Rooks!

17:44.540 --> 17:45.240
What?

17:45.240 --> 17:46.800
Magic doesn't work?

17:47.990 --> 17:52.300
Created by the tower as guardians 
for the first floor, I give you the Zoctonia.

17:52.810 --> 17:57.310
If you focus simply on individual power,
 they'd be worth thirty credits.

17:57.670 --> 18:00.890
They rival monsters from the 
late middle floors of the dungeon.

18:02.570 --> 18:06.150
We can't defeat these! After we made it 
to the tower and everything!

18:06.540 --> 18:10.110
For mages fresh out of the academy, 
they are impossible to defeat.

18:10.870 --> 18:15.410
Their dual shields will reflect 
any perfunctory magic.

18:15.910 --> 18:17.850
Lottl Hjelsnow!

18:26.170 --> 18:27.920
Ars Weiss!

18:30.420 --> 18:32.420
Glace Itier!

18:32.420 --> 18:35.430
Two Zoctonia down in a flash?

18:35.740 --> 18:39.320
Since the Grand Magic Festival, 
his proficiency has drastically increased.

18:39.810 --> 18:44.180
To think that he can control 
your cloning magic to this extent...

18:45.060 --> 18:48.750
Out of them all, 
this one's a cut above the rest.

18:45.690 --> 18:50.650
<b>Wind Faction Aide-de-Camp
Monica Orphan</b>

18:45.690 --> 18:50.650
<b>Head of the Wind Faction
Irwin Aurus</b>

18:48.750 --> 18:52.440
With all that, he'd be an immediate 
asset if we brought him into the faction.

18:52.770 --> 18:56.320
Why was someone 
of his caliber not scouted?

18:53.030 --> 18:56.320
<b>Dark Faction</b>

18:56.320 --> 18:59.340
<i>That's right! I'm a genius!</i>

18:59.340 --> 19:03.220
<i>I can use cloning magic,
 and I'm a beautiful young nobleman!</i>

19:03.220 --> 19:06.310
<i>Comparing me 
to this riffraff is ridiculous!</i>

19:06.310 --> 19:09.170
<i>I should have been scouted!</i>

19:09.170 --> 19:09.840
<i>You see?</i>

19:10.270 --> 19:13.770
<i>This is how beautiful I am! 
This is how brilliant I am!</i>

19:13.770 --> 19:17.590
<i>So, Lady Elfaria, please look at me!</i>

19:20.350 --> 19:23.010
<i>But why?!</i>

19:23.010 --> 19:24.630
<i>Was it the Grand Magic Festival?!</i>

19:24.630 --> 19:29.860
<i>Is it because I was rude and 
tormented the no-talent?!</i>

19:29.900 --> 19:33.650
<b>Head of the Earth Faction
Worguns Prehnite</b>

19:30.140 --> 19:34.730
If he didn't have ice magic, 
we'd have scouted him immediately!

19:34.610 --> 19:36.860
<b>Earth Faction Aide-de-Camp
Frune Owdatid</b>

19:34.730 --> 19:36.620
Indeed, if it weren't for the ice.

19:36.620 --> 19:38.870
What a waste.

19:37.070 --> 19:38.870
<b>Earth Faction Aide-de-Camp
Hammon Fossilis</b>

19:38.870 --> 19:40.870
<i>Blast it!</i>

19:41.450 --> 19:46.870
Other than that ice guy, 
I don't see any promising mages.

19:47.260 --> 19:53.630
No... For better or worse,
there's one more attracting attention.

19:59.510 --> 20:02.890
You're just dodging! 
What are you doing, laggard?!

20:02.890 --> 20:04.890
He's wrong. That's...

20:05.250 --> 20:06.890
He's watching.

20:07.420 --> 20:09.590
Kiki, let me do this on my own.

20:11.220 --> 20:15.490
<i>That sad expression earlier... 
This is what it was about, right, Elfie?</i>

20:16.030 --> 20:18.490
<i>You were saying, 
"I'm sorry I couldn't scout you."</i>

20:19.590 --> 20:21.240
<i>But it's all right.</i>

20:21.770 --> 20:25.200
<i>I'll make it to where you are 
on my own two legs!</i>

20:38.260 --> 20:39.220
He's fast!

20:39.220 --> 20:41.080
No, more than that...

20:39.380 --> 20:41.840
<b>Elf Faction Aide-de-Camp
Filvis Challia</b>

20:39.380 --> 20:41.840
<b>Elf Faction Aide-de-Camp
Lefiya Viridis</b>

20:41.080 --> 20:41.840
He's strong.

20:42.160 --> 20:45.350
Splitting a Zoctonia in two 
from above its shields...

20:42.430 --> 20:45.350
<b>Fire Faction Aide-de-Camp
Logwell</b>

20:45.350 --> 20:48.680
He's even seen through every one
of his opponent's moves.

20:45.930 --> 20:49.850
<b>Lightning Faction Aide-de-Camp
Guilford Zurgas</b>

20:48.680 --> 20:50.310
And in so short a time?

20:50.770 --> 20:53.110
<i>I've already seen that attack!</i>

20:54.260 --> 20:56.650
<i>I can see my opponent's moves
more clearly than before!</i>

20:57.110 --> 20:59.370
<i>This Gloria is so flexible and light!</i>

20:59.370 --> 21:01.360
<i>It's so easy to move around in!</i>

21:01.360 --> 21:03.870
<i>This blade Mister Donnan forged
can cut through everything!</i>

21:04.180 --> 21:07.750
<i>Right now, I feel like I can do anything!</i>

21:12.510 --> 21:14.130
There's still more coming?!

21:16.250 --> 21:18.130
Glace Itier!

21:19.220 --> 21:20.300
Not good!

21:20.300 --> 21:21.180
A stray shot is—

21:21.930 --> 21:23.970
Julius, sorry! I'm gonna borrow this!

21:33.190 --> 21:35.090
Fully Charged...

21:36.010 --> 21:37.600
Glauss Wis!

21:37.940 --> 21:39.000
Will!

21:40.950 --> 21:42.100
Load!

21:42.100 --> 21:43.110
Burst!

21:47.300 --> 21:48.950
Glauss Mill!

23:28.010 --> 23:30.970
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

23:36.620 --> 23:39.440
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.440 --> 23:43.760
episode 19, "He Said He Would 
No Longer Hang His Head."

23:40.440 --> 23:45.950
Episode 19
He Said He Would No Longer Hang His Head
